{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
[Em]When I was a little lad
And [D]so my mother told me,
[Em]Way, haul away, we'll [D]haul away, [Em]Joe!
That [Em]if I did not kiss the girls
My [D]lips would all grow mouldy,
[Em]Way, haul away, we'll [D]haul away, [Em]Joe!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
[Em]King Louis was the king of France
Be[D]fore the revolution,
[Em]Way, haul away, we'll [D]haul away, [Em]Joe!
But [Em]then he got his head cut off,
Which [D]spoiled his constitution,
[Em]Way, haul away, we'll [D]haul away, [Em]Joe!
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: Em}
